	When set to non-zero, indicates the capability to receive video using AL1.
field	tSM_UT32 video_with_AL1 in	
	When set to non-zero, indicates the capability to receive video using AL2.
field	tSM_UT32 video_with_AL2 in
	When set to non-zero, indicates the capability to receive video using AL3.
field	tSM_UT32 video_with_AL3 in
	When set to non-zero, indicates the capability to receive audio using AL1.
field	tSM_UT32 audio_with_AL1 in	
	When set to non-zero, indicates the capability to receive audio using AL2.
field	tSM_UT32 audio_with_AL2 in
	When set to non-zero, indicates the capability to receive audio using AL3.
field	tSM_UT32 audio_with_AL3 in
	When set to non-zero, indicates the capability to receive data using AL1.
field	tSM_UT32 data_with_AL1 in	
	When set to non-zero, indicates the capability to receive data using AL2.
field	tSM_UT32 data_with_AL2 in
	When set to non-zero, indicates the capability to receive data using AL3.
field	tSM_UT32 data_with_AL3 in
	Indicates the maximum number of octets in each SDU that the terminal can receive when
	using adaptation layer type 2.
field	tSM_INT maximum_AL2_sdu_size in
	Indicates the maximum number of octets in each SDU that the terminal can receive when
	using adaptation layer type 3.
field	tSM_INT maximum_AL3_sdu_size in
	Indicates the maximum peak-to-peak multiplexing jitter that the transmitter shall cause.
	Measured in milliseconds.
field	tSM_INT maximum_delay_jitter in	
	When set to non-zero, indicates that the transmitter is able to restrict the size of the
	H.223 MUX-PDUs that it transmits.  Has no meaning when part of a receive capability.
field	tSM_UT32 max_MUX_PDU_size_capability in
	When set to non-zero, indicates support of the Annex A/H.324 NSRP mode.
field	tSM_UT32 nsrp_support in
	Indicates the bit rate to transmit the bitstream output from the H.223 multiplexer.  Please
	note that this parameter is optional.
field	tSM_INT bit_rate_o in	

	The parameters in this structure indicate the capability to transmit the multiplex layers
	described in Annex A/H.223 and Annex B/H.223.  Please note that this structure is optional.
