	Fetch status info on H.223 mux
apifn	sm_h223mux_status
params	sm_h223mux_status_parms statusp
	The mux.
field	tSMH223muxId h223mux in
enumstart kSMH223muxStatus
	The H.223 session is running.
enum	kSMH223muxStatusRunning
	The H.223 session has stopped and it is now safe to destroy.
enum	kSMH223muxStatusStopped
	H.223 session has started and the setup level has been negotiated successfully.
enum	kSMH223muxStatusSessionStarted
	H.223 session creation has failed.
enum	kSMH223muxStatusCreateSessionFailed
	H.223 session deletion has failed.
enum	kSMH223muxStatusDeleteSessionFailed
	The setting of terminal capabilities has failed.
enum	kSMH223muxStatusSetCapsFailed
	Multiplex table entry addition has failed.
enum	kSMH223muxStatusAddEntryFailed	
	Open logical channel request has failed.
enum	kSMH223muxStatusOpenLCFailed
	Close logical channel request has failed.
enum	kSMH223muxStatusCloseLCFailed	
	Level has changed as a result of a reconfiguration request.
enum	kSMH223muxStatusReconfigLevelChange	
	Multiplex reconfiguration request has failed.
enum	kSMH223muxStatusReconfigFailed	
	The H.223 session encountered one or more internal errors during processing.  These
	errors are likely to result in missing data.  Note that such errors are not fatal
	and the H.223 session will continue to run.  These status reports are throttled in 
	order to maintain a sensibly low rate of reporting even in the event of a high rate
	of errors.
enum	kSMH223muxStatusInternalError	
	The video logical channel has entered a busy situation and will now drop all subsequent
	P-frames added to the transmit queue until an I-frame is received.
enum	kSMH223muxStatusVideoPFrameDrop
	An I-frame has been received on the video channel queue after entering a busy situation,
	so subsequent P-frames will now be sent.
enum	kSMH223muxStatusVideoPFrameSend	
enumend status out
	Additional information relating to the current status of the H.223 mux.
